\ Deadline (Infocom, 1982), translated from its ZIL source into telic.
\
\   ./telic examples/deadline.telic [text] [dark] [seed=N] [width=N] [save=path] [frotz=N]
\
\ You are the inspector called to the Robner estate at 8:00 am to look into
\ the death of Marshall Robner; you have until 8:00 pm. Type commands as in
\ any Infocom game: LOOK, NORTH, TAKE THE CUP, EXAMINE THE DESK, ASK MRS.
\ ROBNER ABOUT THE WILL, WAIT UNTIL 11:30, SAVE, QUIT; GRAMMAR lists every
\ verb and the sentences it takes, and every synonym. The game runs in a
\ window: the status line, a picture of the room with the people in it, and
\ the story below; up and down scroll the story, as page up and page down do
\ by half a screen, shift with up and down recalls commands, escape ends. The
\ pictures are ink on paper before 6:00 pm and light on black after; dark
\ draws them all as light on black. text runs it in the terminal instead.
\ seed=N fixes the random
\ numbers, so the same commands replay the same story; width=N wraps the
\ terminal's text at N columns (0 does not wrap); save=path names the file
\ SAVE and RESTORE use (deadline.save by default). frotz=N draws the random
\ numbers as the interpreter frotz does when started with -s N, and words
\ questions as under its status line, so a transcript can be compared line by
\ line with the original game's (release 28, whose source this is).
\
\ The world is in examples/deadline/: the rooms and things (rooms.telic,
\ objects.telic), the vocabulary and sentence patterns (vocabulary.telic,
\ grammar.telic), the parser, the clock, the people, the actions (verbs.telic),
\ what the rooms do (places.telic), how the people move and act (movement.telic,
\ characters.telic), the day's events and the endings (plot.telic), what the
\ things do (things.telic) and the turn loop (game.telic). The pictures are
\ drawn by wireframe.telic, the people by figures.telic, the rooms by
\ scenes.telic and scenes-*.telic, and the window is screen.telic. In the
\ window the game has a cool-jazz soundtrack on the synthesizer: the pieces
\ are music.telic, the sounds of the places ambience.telic, and
\ soundtrack.telic chooses what plays when.

"deadline/text.telic" load
"deadline/world.telic" load
"deadline/vocabulary.telic" load
"deadline/rooms.telic" load
"deadline/objects.telic" load
"deadline/grammar.telic" load
complete-vocabulary
"deadline/parser.telic" load
"deadline/clock.telic" load
"deadline/people.telic" load
"deadline/verbs.telic" load
"deadline/places.telic" load
"deadline/movement.telic" load
"deadline/characters.telic" load
"deadline/plot.telic" load
"deadline/things.telic" load
"deadline/help.telic" load
"deadline/game.telic" load

\ text runs the game in the terminal; otherwise it runs in a window with the room pictures
args "text" position-of 0 >= to text-mode
( text-mode not if
	"deadline/wireframe.telic" load
	"deadline/figures.telic" load
	"deadline/scenes.telic" load
	"deadline/scenes-grounds.telic" load
	"deadline/scenes-ground-floor.telic" load
	"deadline/scenes-upstairs.telic" load
	"deadline/scenes-bedrooms.telic" load
	"deadline/screen.telic" load
	"deadline/music.telic" load
	"deadline/ambience.telic" load
	"deadline/soundtrack.telic" load
then ) execute

\ the value of an argument name=value, or a default
: argument ( name default -- value )
	| name default |
	args ( argument | argument "^" name + "=" + has? ) find-first to given
	given null? if default exit then
	given "^[^=]*=" "" replace ;

"seed" "1" argument string>number to game-seed
"width" "79" argument string>number to line-width
"save" "deadline.save" argument to save-path
"frotz" "" argument to frotz-seed
( ^frotz-random ^status-line-shown |
	frotz-seed "" = not if
		frotz-seed string>number float>exact to frotz-random
		true to status-line-shown
	then
) execute

open-display
play
close-display
